      "signpost": null,
      "definition": "added to a noun to make an adjective meaning similar to that thing, or typical of it",
      "explanation": "Common words are written as one word (*childlike*, *lifelike*, *businesslike*). Less common or new combinations usually take a hyphen (*a star-like shape*), and so does a word that ends in **l** (*a bell-like sound*).",
